Vercel Web Analytics Installation Complete

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this React portfolio project.

## Implementation Summary

### 1. Documentation Research
Fetched the latest installation instructions from the official Vercel documentation:
https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart

This ensured we used the most up-to-date framework-specific integration steps.

### 2. Framework Identification
Identified the project as a React application built with Create React App (react-scripts 5.0.1).

### 3. Package Installation
Installed the `@vercel/analytics` package (version 2.0.1) using npm with the `--legacy-peer-deps` flag to resolve peer dependency conflicts with the existing TypeScript version.

Command used:
```
npm install @vercel/analytics --legacy-peer-deps
```

### 4. Code Integration
Following the official documentation for React applications, added the Analytics component to the application:

**Modified File: `src/App.js`**
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/react";`
- Added `<Analytics />` component inside the main app container, after the Routes component
- Placement ensures the analytics component is included on all pages while respecting the dark mode container

### 5. Verification
- ✅ Build completed successfully with no errors
- ✅ Package.json updated with @vercel/analytics dependency
- ✅ Package-lock.json updated with all transitive dependencies
- ✅ No linting errors introduced (build passed ESLint checks)
- ✅ Code structure preserved and existing functionality maintained

## Files Modified

1. **package.json** - Added `@vercel/analytics` to dependencies
2. **package-lock.json** - Updated with new dependency tree
3. **src/App.js** - Added Analytics import and component

## Next Steps

To complete the Vercel Web Analytics setup:

1. Deploy this updated code to Vercel
2. Enable Web Analytics in your Vercel dashboard:
   - Navigate to your project in the Vercel dashboard
   - Click "Analytics" in the sidebar
   - Click the "Enable" button
3. After deployment, analytics will automatically start tracking page views

## Notes

- The Analytics component was placed inside the Router component to ensure it works correctly with React Router
- The component is placed after the Routes to avoid interfering with navigation
- Analytics will work in both production and development modes, but data collection is optimized for production
- No additional configuration is required; the component will automatically track page views and Web Vitals
